== Everything Is Terrible!!! changes ==
{{hatnote|See also: [[Everything is Terrible 2!!!]]}}
After beating Mom's Heart 5 times, the following playthroughs have the following changes:

* Bosses drop 1 less health pickup.
* The chance of a floor receiving a [[curses|curse]] increases.
* {{Dlc+|r}} The {{e|Bulb}} enemy can appear.{{dlc-}}
* {{Dlc|r}} Unlocks {{e|Half Soul Heart|n}}s.
* {{Dlc|r}} Unlocks {{e|Micro Battery|text=Micro Batteries|n}}.

== Notes ==
* Every time Mom's Heart is defeated changes the current [[Savefile Images|savefile's image]] until It Lives! is unlocked.
* Until It Lives! is unlocked, Mom's Heart cannot be continued past unless a {{r|Devil Room}} or an {{r|Angel Room}} appears, which allows access to {{s|Sheol}} or the {{s|Cathedral}}, respectively.
* Just like Mom, using {{i|The Bible}} or {{p|XV - The Devil?}} against '''Mom's Heart''' will kill it instantly.
* If {{i|Forget Me Now}} or a 5 pip {{r|Dice Room}} is used on {{S|Womb}} II / {{S|Utero}} II / {{S|Scarred Womb|na+}} II after defeating {{e|Mom's Heart}}, and Mom's Heart is again defeated on the regenerated floor, it will count as having defeated Mom's Heart 2 separate times, therefore unlocking 2 consequent [[endings]].
* {{dlc+|r}} Erasing {{s|Mausoleum}} / {{s|Gehenna}} Mom's Heart with the {{i|Eraser}} will not open the passage to {{s|Corpse}}.{{dlc-}}

== Trivia ==
* Mom's Heart appeared in the original ''The Binding of Isaac.''
** In the original ''Binding Of Isaac'', the only attack Mom's Heart could perform was spawning 2-4 monsters before disappearing and repeating the same move each time the wave of monsters were killed off.
* The music that plays during this fight is titled [https://ridiculon.bandcamp.com/track/ventricide-womb-fight ''Ventricide'']. Ventricide is a made-up word formed from the word ventricle (one of the two larger chambers of the heart) and the suffix -cide, which denotes an act of killing. This theme is used in other tracks, such as Matricide, Hericide, and Infanticide.
** Ventricide could also be a junction of the prefix ''ventr-'' (from the latin word ''venter''), which could denote "belly", "stomach", "womb" or "fetus", with the suffix ''-cide''.
** Mom's Heart shares this theme with It Lives!.
* {{Dlc|nr}} During the versus screen, Mom's Heart's enemy-spawning sound can be heard. Mom's Heart is one of {{Dlc|nr}} seven / {{Dlc|r}} five bosses that can be heard during the versus screen, the other {{Dlc|nr}} six / {{Dlc|r}} four being {{e|The Stain}}, {{e|The Forsaken}}, {{e|Big Horn}}, Mom, {{dlc|nr}} It Lives!, and {{e|Mother}}.
* {{dlc|r}} The floor graphic beneath Isaac and Mom's Heart in the boss VS Screen in Mausoleum/Gehenna is of a slightly lighter shade of red than in the {{s|Womb}}.
** In addition to this, despite having a Womb backdrop, Mom's Heart's room in the Mausoleum/Gehenna does not have the red static effect of the Womb.
* Getting killed by the final ring of projectiles released after killing Mom's Heart will play the respective ending if there is one, and will count as a Mom's Heart kill. However, it is still considered a loss and will not count towards a win streak.
* {{dlc+|r}} Originally in ''Antibirth'', the {{s|Mausoleum}} version of Mom's Heart could spawn enemies like {{e|Bouncer}}s and {{e|Blurb}}s.{{dlc-}}
* Isaac consistently killing Mom's Heart, followed by the first appearances of the Ending Chest, could represent how his death hurt his mother. Considering how in the Final Ending after defeating {{E|The Beast}}, Isaac's Mom can be seen heartbroken about her son's demise.

